WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.451 --> 00:00:05.291
- There's a lot of places
that don't let me perform

00:00:05.291 --> 00:00:07.151
simply because I'm black.

00:00:07.151 --> 00:00:09.872
That doesn't really get
to me because I'm trying

00:00:09.872 --> 00:00:12.080
to show the world that, you know, music is universal,

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.280
it can unite us all.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.863
(upbeat music)

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.061
My name is Rhyan Lowery, and I'm also known

00:00:21.061 --> 00:00:22.232
as El Compa Negro.

00:00:22.232 --> 00:00:25.512
El Compa Negro simply
means the black friend.

00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:28.719
I sing Regional Musica Mexicana, Banda,

00:00:28.719 --> 00:00:31.052
Sierreño, Norteño, Mariachi.

00:00:38.447 --> 00:00:40.865
Since I was little, I've
been around Hispanics,

00:00:40.865 --> 00:00:44.948
so it actually comes
natural in me, it flows out.

00:00:45.815 --> 00:00:48.173
I grew up in the streets of Compton.

00:00:48.173 --> 00:00:50.339
I lived in a neighborhood
that was predominantly

00:00:50.339 --> 00:00:52.455
black and Mexican.

00:00:52.455 --> 00:00:55.393
It's a wonderful thing to
say, you know, ”I came from Compton."

00:00:55.393 --> 00:00:57.783
Because they say a lot of
people don't make it out.

00:00:57.783 --> 00:00:59.844
I've traveled to a lot of places

00:00:59.844 --> 00:01:01.427
and I'm all over TV,

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:03.752
and I can say,

00:01:03.752 --> 00:01:06.306
"Hey, I'm from Compton."

00:01:06.306 --> 00:01:07.139
A lot of people tell me,

00:01:07.139 --> 00:01:08.205
"Hey, you're supposed to be Mexican,

00:01:08.205 --> 00:01:10.016
"God just left you in the oven too long."

00:01:10.016 --> 00:01:11.485
(laughing)

00:01:11.485 --> 00:01:13.915
I know for a fact that
I am African American,

00:01:13.915 --> 00:01:16.106
but, yeah, I do feel
like I live that life.

00:01:16.106 --> 00:01:17.706
I have lived the ranchero life.

00:01:17.706 --> 00:01:20.242
I've had horses, I've had roosters, goats,

00:01:20.242 --> 00:01:21.245
eggs, everything.

00:01:21.245 --> 00:01:22.725
I know how to saddle up a horse,

00:01:22.725 --> 00:01:24.438
get on there, make him
dance and everything.

00:01:24.438 --> 00:01:26.595
A lot of people misunderstand and say,

00:01:26.595 --> 00:01:28.088
"Hey, you're trying to
be Mexican too much."

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:30.438
I'm like, "Well, there
are American cowboys."

00:01:30.438 --> 00:01:32.379
There are people who use boots.

00:01:32.379 --> 00:01:35.557
That's what I was taught,
what I've been around.

00:01:35.557 --> 00:01:37.299
But, yes, like I said in my song--

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:39.882
(horse neighs)

00:01:43.797 --> 00:01:44.979
But like I said in my song,

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:47.191
I have the heart and soul of a Mexican.

00:01:47.191 --> 00:01:51.024
I think that that pretty
much is what counts.

